nesses: regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills, hot temper, regarded as a know-it-all, moody, loner. So responsibility, concentration, problem solving strong, but attitude issues.\n\nNow we need to decide best overall fit. All have issues. Which candidate has the best balance? Let's weigh criteria importance: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, professional communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nCandidate B: reliability (very conscientious), stress resilience (handles stress well), technical competence (good at assessing weather, computer skills), decision quality unknown, attention unknown, crew cooperation (pretentious, wrong tone, uncooperative), communication issues, adaptability unknown.\n\nCandidate A: technical competence (anticipates danger, complex connections, spatial vision), decision quality maybe, leadership, but reliability questionable (unorganized), stress resilience unknown, crew cooperation (show-off, unfriendly), adaptability (not open to new ideas), responsibility maybe.\n\nCandidate C: reliability (100%), decision quality (quick correct decisions), crew cooperation (positive atmosphere), but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability), technical competence unknown.\n\nCandidate D: responsibility, concentration, problem solving, handles unexpected events, but attitude issues (arrogance, hot temper, know-it-all, moody, loner) affecting crew cooperation and communication.\n\nWhich is best? B seems strong on reliability and stress, which are critical. Communication issues are concerning but maybe less severe than hot temper or egocentric. D's hot temper could be dangerous. A's technical strengths are important for long-distance, but his inability to take criticism and being unorganized could affect reliability. C's reliability and positive atmosphere are good, but egocentric and communication issues.\n\nI think B is the most balanced: high reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, and while communication style is off, it may be manageable. So I might align with Agent 3's recommendation for B.\n\nThus I will support Candidate B, perhaps reinforcing with additional facts: B is very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), but pretentious and wrong tone (communication). I can argue that these communication issues are less safety-critical than A's inability to take criticism and D's hot temper.\n\nThus my vote: Candidate B.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: reference prior discussion (Agent 2 argued for A, Agent 3 for B). I will say I agree with Agent 3, and explain why B is best.\n\nInclude explicit facts: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, pretentious, wrong tone.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B."}
